 - **Request event.** Carries model, effort, `toolsHash`, `systemHash`, `bodyHash`, TTL and header names with value hashes. Never header values.
 - **Role fallback** starts a new session on the fallback model; it never swaps the model inside a session (cache rule 5).
-- **Quota fallback.** A run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns.
+- **Quota fallback.** A run that ends on a `quota` error continues on its fallback model (`--fallback`, then `fallback` in `~/.cedia/settings.json`, then the built-in `deepseek` → `anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5`; `none` turns it off; a repo cannot set it). The new session has `parentSession`, a logged reminder that the tree may hold part of the work, what is left of the turn and budget limits, and the first session's changed files as writes the done gate must still see verified. The result adds up both sessions' spend and turns. `--on-quota wait:<minutes>` (or `onQuota` in user settings; default `fallback`) waits in the same session instead, for a 429 with a retry-after, up to that many minutes across the run, and falls back only past it. Each wait is a logged `attempt`, with a stderr line. A spent balance names no time and falls back at once.
+- **Refused history.** A `bad_request` or `context_length` after the session's first accepted request means the provider refuses the history itself, and a resend fails the same way. The run goes on once in a new session on the same model, as quota fallback does (`parentSession`, the changed files, a logged note), recorded as `why: 'rejected'`. A resumed thread whose last session was refused starts a new one.
